Package: daisyr
Title: Sensitivity Analysis and Calibration Tools for the Daisy Model
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Mohamed Jabloun", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "daisyr@example.com")
Description: Tools for driving the Daisy agroecosystem model (soil-crop-water-
    nitrogen simulation) from R. Provides a YAML parameters file for describing
    free parameters (including piecewise linear function shape parameters)
    that live inside one or more '.dai' setup files, template rendering to
    generate concrete '.dai' files, helpers to run the Daisy executable and
    parse its '.dlf' log output, generic objective functions for comparing
    simulated to observed data, decoupled Morris/Sobol sensitivity analysis,
    DEoptim-based calibration (also BOBYQA, multi-BOBYQA, DDS, and CMA-ES), space-filling metamodel designs, and Kriging /
    EGO surrogate-assisted calibration workflows built on top of these
    primitives.
